From a3792a49888b0dddaab65db2be8ce1cc913127ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:07:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 074/240] Bugfix: apply left shifts to unsigned integers in
 remaining bit sets [report R. Perry]

Commit 6a00c51 made the bit-set left shifts unsigned in the ordering and
mapping modules, but left the generic `flagSize'/`flagVal'/`flagSet' macros
in common.h operating on signed `int' arrays with `(1 << bit)'. When the
flagged vertex index is 31 modulo 32, `1 << 31' shifts into the sign bit of
`int', which is undefined behaviour. These macros are used by the PT-Scotch
bipartitioners `bdgraphBipartEx()' and `bdgraphBipartBd()'; their flag arrays
are changed from `int' to `unsigned int' accordingly.

Refs: GRA-16
